<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>ai.ted.sweep</string>

  <!-- The product checks, once a day, silent unless something moved.

       ai.ted.gatewatch runs ted-watch.py every fifteen minutes and watches the
       machine: gates, link, model, power, credit. Every check in it was
       written after an outage. The checks this runs are the other half, the
       ones about people rather than processes, and until now not one of them
       ran unless somebody remembered to type it. On 3 Sep 2026 a user asked to
       be forgotten; `npm run deletion:audit` would have said so on any day
       since, and it was sixteen days before anybody looked.

       09:00 rather than the small hours, because unlike a backup this is meant
       to be read. It lands before the day starts rather than at the bottom of
       an overnight inbox. Every fifteen minutes would be wrong for a different
       reason: none of these numbers can move faster than a person can act on
       them, and the cost of asking is a full 30-day scan and a Convex round
       trip.

       RunAtLoad is false. The first run of the day writes the baseline the
       second compares against, and a run on every login would compare the
       morning to twenty minutes ago and have nothing to say.

       The interpreter is the Hermes venv's, not /usr/bin/python3, and that is
       not a preference: macOS refuses a launchd agent access to ~/Documents
       unless that binary has been granted it, and the Command Line Tools
       python has not. See the same note in ai.ted.backup.plist, which was
       written after that failure. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/Documents/build-week-health accountability partner/scripts/ted-sweep.py</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>9</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>0</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/logs/ted-sweep.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/logs/ted-sweep.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
